WEBVTT

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:09.840
Call the meeting of<br/>the Board of Directors,

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:17.180
Dallas College, May 12,<br/>4 p.m. at 418. I confirm that

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:18.620
we do have a quorum present.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:24.720
In accordance with Chapter 551 of<br/>the Texas Open Meetings Act,

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:26.980
I call to order the regular meeting<br/>of the Board of Trustees,

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:29.640
Dallas College, for May 12, 2026.

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:31.900
At 419 p.m.

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:33.900
Members of the public who<br/>have followed the instructions

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:37.780
on the Dallas College Board of Trustees<br/>website for registering to speak

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:40.880
during the public<br/>comment portion will be given five minutes.

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:44.979
This regular board meeting is being held in<br/>person and broadcast over the Internet.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.400
Audio recording and transcripts of<br/>this meeting are

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:51.140
being made and will be available to<br/>the public on the Board's website after the

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:54.360
meeting at a later date. Chancellor,<br/>can you please confirm this meeting is

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:56.240
posted in accordance with the law?

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:58.700
Mr. Chair, I can certify that this<br/>meeting has been posted in

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:01.640
accordance with Section 551.054 of<br/>the Texas Government Code.

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:12.380
I pledge allegiance to the flag of<br/>the United States of America,

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:18.640
to the republic for which it stands,<br/>one nation, under God, indivisible,

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:20.860
with liberty and justice for all.

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:26.660
I honor the Texas flag.<br/>I pledge allegiance to the Texas,

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:30.540
one state, under God, one president.

00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:45.810
We have some folks desiring to speak<br/>to the Board this evening,

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:49.010
so let me make this announcement.

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:52.350
Persons who address the Board are reminded<br/>that the Board may not take

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:54.970
formal action on matters that are not<br/>part of the meeting agenda.

00:01:54.970 --> 00:01:57.830
And may not discuss or<br/>deliberate on any topic

00:01:57.830 --> 00:02:02.090
that is not specifically named in the<br/>agenda that was posted to be business days

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:03.550
in advance of the meeting today.

00:02:04.370 --> 00:02:06.870
For any agenda topic that is<br/>introduced during this meeting,

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:09.070
there are only three permissible responses.

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:12.290
Provide a factual answer to<br/>a question to cite

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:17.150
specific Board or Trustee policy relevant to<br/>the topic or to place the topic on

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:18.510
the agenda of a subsequent meeting.

00:02:19.190 --> 00:02:21.930
Speakers shall direct their presentations<br/>only to the Board

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:25.310
Chair or the Board as a whole,<br/>and shall confine comments to the

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:28.169
agenda items about which<br/>they have requested to speak to the Board.

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:32.210
Maximum time limit for all<br/>comments is five minutes.

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:34.730
The Board reserves the right to<br/>limit the maximum allowable time.

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:43.060
Presentations... I'm going to call<br/>Dr. Daniel Diaz.

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:22.800
Good afternoon. My name is Dr. Daniel Diaz.<br/>I am a former student here.

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:27.460
I'm here today as a private citizen to<br/>talk about the subject

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:29.500
of institutional accountability.

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:35.720
In the May 2nd,<br/>2023 Pace Campus Climate Survey,

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:41.400
Dallas College's own employees said,<br/>in their own words, one employee wrote,

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:42.120
and I quote,

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:45.300
The lack of opportunity to move<br/>up in this organization

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:50.300
is frustrating. I like the work that I do,<br/>but my direct supervisor makes

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:51.920
the work environment difficult.

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:56.200
Another one wrote,<br/>We already have the technology

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:59.760
and talent to fix this place up,<br/>but they're not utilized.

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:04.920
And another one wrote,<br/>I'm usually not the one to complain about

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:08.720
my pay because I used to think it was fair,<br/>but I've been doing more than two full

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:10.280
time jobs for a while now.

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:14.920
Partly because no one else will take<br/>one for the tragic salary offered.

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:20.420
Again, these are Dallas College<br/>employees back in 2023.

00:04:21.779 --> 00:04:24.880
This, well,<br/>Dallas College built an administrative

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:30.360
court of about 420 employees,<br/>the majority earning six-figure salaries.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:38.360
Now, this is more six-figure salaries within<br/>those 420 employees than Tarrant County,

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:42.440
Collin County College,<br/>and Lone Star College combined.

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:44.540
Now, Lone Star College,<br/>I want to remind you,

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:46.580
is the largest system in the state.

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:50.660
That is not a perception problem.<br/>That is a resource allocation decision

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:52.900
made deliberately by design.

00:04:53.779 --> 00:04:56.900
That same survey gave institutional<br/>structure its lowest score,

00:04:57.600 --> 00:04:59.560
839 critical comments.

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:04.940
And yet, at the April 7,<br/>2026 regular board meeting,

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:08.240
timestamped 58 minutes and 34 seconds,<br/>the Chancellor said,

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:10.720
and I quote directly from<br/>the caption record,

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:12.160
from the official caption record,

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:16.600
quote, those people may be<br/>hesitating for whatever reason.

00:05:17.060 --> 00:05:19.360
Don't. We want to hear from you.

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:24.520
Again, we can't fix and address what<br/>we don't know. So please,

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:26.240
please, please.

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:29.980
I just encourage everyone to<br/>participate in that,

00:05:29.980 --> 00:05:33.640
unquote. Please, please, please.

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:38.120
About a survey. Quote,<br/>we want to hear from you, unquote.

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:40.839
The problem is no one is listening.

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:48.120
This institution, its employees,<br/>and the communities you serve,

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:53.760
know that you do not reassure people<br/>about fears that do not exist.

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:57.279
When employees fear providing<br/>accurate information

00:05:57.279 --> 00:06:00.660
on an institutional survey,<br/>that fear is so culturally embedded,

00:06:00.820 --> 00:06:05.500
so real, so experienced that even a<br/>Chancellor's public reassurance provides

00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:07.060
insufficient protection.

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:10.560
That's concerning. That chilling effect<br/>is not a perception.

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:13.779
It is documented in your own records<br/>at your own board meetings.

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:17.839
The board has approved at<br/>least eight settlements in

00:06:17.839 --> 00:06:23.080
the last six years alone for discrimination,<br/>retaliation, and similar matters,

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:27.300
funded by public taxpayer dollars<br/>under non-disclosure agreements

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:29.760
that violate Dallas College's<br/>own written policy.

00:06:31.279 --> 00:06:33.180
Interestingly, those settlements<br/>and lawsuits

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:36.260
are nowhere to be<br/>found in past agendas and

00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:39.500
minutes. Eight settlements,<br/>eight silenced voices,

00:06:39.640 --> 00:06:42.120
all defended by the same outside law firm.

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:47.000
The college was defended by the same<br/>law firm that has billed you

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:50.420
a million dollars in the last<br/>six years. One million dollars.

00:06:51.279 --> 00:06:56.400
And you paid $250,000<br/>in settlements to at least eight individuals

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:57.740
in the last six years.

00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:04.080
The same firms defending plaintiffs and<br/>defendants engaged in this circus.

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:08.820
And while those settlements were being paid,<br/>Dallas College's own check

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:12.640
registers document over<br/>$4 million in anomalous vendor payments.

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:18.080
How do you justify $18,000<br/>spent at the Ritz Carlton,

00:07:18.140 --> 00:07:19.280
coded as seminar fees?

00:07:20.020 --> 00:07:24.420
How do you justify over $100,000<br/>within the last five years spent at

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:28.780
the Albany PGA Frisco Resort,<br/>coded as conference expenses?

00:07:29.640 --> 00:07:35.520
Private shared services billed to a<br/>public community college. $711,000

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:36.780
in limousine services.

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:41.420
And the list goes on and on.<br/>I've documented it here for you,

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:45.900
just to make it easier,<br/>but there are some concerning things here.

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:52.720
There is a $35,000<br/>payment to a Christian camp. Camp Cho Yeh,

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:55.740
it advertises itself as a Christian retreat.

00:07:55.740 --> 00:08:00.420
That is concerning. That you<br/>would use public

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:03.160
funds to pay for a Christian retreat.

00:08:04.740 --> 00:08:08.660
And there are over a million dollars,<br/>actually $1.5 million,

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:13.400
spent at different Hyatt properties,<br/>including resorts.

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:17.120
Some of these payments with<br/>the Ash Limousine

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:20.320
service are coded across<br/>nine different categories.

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:23.760
Dr. Diaz, sum up these five.

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:26.080
Yep. Well, I am going to<br/>leave you with these three

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:28.220
questions that I know you don't<br/>have to answer today,

00:08:28.220 --> 00:08:29.620
but I hope you one day do.

00:08:30.120 --> 00:08:34.140
Who authorized over $4 million in<br/>this anomalous vendor payments?

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:37.640
How does an institution that<br/>prohibits NDAs in its

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:40.260
own written policy enter into<br/>a confidential settlement?

00:08:41.960 --> 00:08:44.080
And third,<br/>which of you will have the integrity

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:46.260
to hold those who designed<br/>the system accountable?

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:49.880
Now, if I may approach the board,<br/>I would like to leave you with a

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:51.860
copy of what I just covered.

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:54.640
You can leave it with...

00:09:02.770 --> 00:09:06.550
Key? Did I do justice to your name?

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:10.130
Well, thank you. I like to do that.

00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:18.210
Hi, you guys. My name is Key. Like you said,<br/>I am the owner and founder of

00:09:18.210 --> 00:09:19.750
Key Academy Hair Weaving School.

00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:20.470
Can you hear me?

00:09:25.070 --> 00:09:30.710
Okay, so we specialize in a high-demand,<br/>fast-track career pathway that

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:34.950
allows students to<br/>become licensed hair wheeling specialists in

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:39.070
as little as 10 to 15 weeks<br/>without attending the traditional

00:09:39.070 --> 00:09:40.270
cosmetology school.

00:09:41.070 --> 00:09:43.970
Today, I am here to<br/>propose a partnership that

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:47.050
brings the opportunity directly<br/>to Dallas College.

00:09:47.050 --> 00:09:52.890
Right now, there is a major gap in<br/>the workforce education within

00:09:52.890 --> 00:09:54.190
the beauty industry.

00:09:54.830 --> 00:09:59.650
Traditional cosmetology programs,<br/>they require at least a thousand hours.

00:10:00.270 --> 00:10:03.210
They take nine months to a year to complete.

00:10:03.750 --> 00:10:06.610
And then they often cost<br/>students a significant

00:10:06.610 --> 00:10:08.650
amount of time and financial commitment.

00:10:09.390 --> 00:10:12.550
But the market has shifted,<br/>and students today are looking

00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:14.450
for faster career pathways,

00:10:14.450 --> 00:10:19.570
lower cost training options,<br/>skills that lead to immediate income.

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:22.690
And at the same time,<br/>the demand for hair extension

00:10:22.690 --> 00:10:26.650
services has exploded,<br/>especially in our communities.

00:10:26.990 --> 00:10:32.550
Yet there are very few structured licensed<br/>training pathways available through college.

00:10:34.390 --> 00:10:36.390
Key Academy solves that gap.

00:10:36.830 --> 00:10:41.570
We offer a 300-hour state<br/>approved hair-weaving specialist program,

00:10:41.929 --> 00:10:44.750
in that it prepares students<br/>for Texas licensing.

00:10:45.410 --> 00:10:48.090
It includes theory and hands-on training.

00:10:48.470 --> 00:10:51.510
It covers installation techniques,<br/>sanitation,

00:10:52.270 --> 00:10:54.230
client consultation, and business skills.

00:10:55.210 --> 00:10:58.670
Our students are not just trained,<br/>they are licensed in workforce training.

00:10:58.670 --> 00:11:03.010
Even more importantly,<br/>graduates can begin to earn at

00:11:03.010 --> 00:11:05.230
least $800 to $2,500<br/>per week.

00:11:05.870 --> 00:11:12.350
Many become entrepreneurs, suite renters,<br/>or independent stylists ready for

00:11:12.350 --> 00:11:17.970
immediate work after completion.

00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:22.290
This is not just education,<br/>this is economic mobility.

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:25.890
This is where Dallas College can come in.

00:11:25.890 --> 00:11:30.890
By integrating our program,<br/>Dallas College can expand workforce programs

00:11:30.890 --> 00:11:33.510
that can add a high<br/>demand beauty certification

00:11:33.510 --> 00:11:35.510
that aligns with a real industry trend,

00:11:36.150 --> 00:11:40.130
that can attract new student<br/>demographics like young entrepreneurs,

00:11:40.929 --> 00:11:41.770
career changers,

00:11:42.090 --> 00:11:45.910
students who may not<br/>pursue traditional degrees,

00:11:47.410 --> 00:11:49.350
increased enrollment and revenue,

00:11:50.030 --> 00:11:52.570
short-term programs with<br/>fast completion cycles,

00:11:52.570 --> 00:11:55.970
high retention due to<br/>career-driven outcomes,

00:11:57.150 --> 00:11:58.530
aligned with workforce funding.

00:11:59.150 --> 00:12:03.110
Programs like WIOA and<br/>Texas Workforce Solutions

00:12:03.110 --> 00:12:05.470
already support training like ours.

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:08.750
This opened doors for<br/>funded tuition opportunities,

00:12:09.190 --> 00:12:11.929
and this partnership positioned<br/>Dallas College as

00:12:11.929 --> 00:12:14.309
a leader in modern skill education.

00:12:15.830 --> 00:12:20.150
I am proposing a collaborative<br/>model where the

00:12:20.150 --> 00:12:22.070
Key Academy can provide the curriculum,

00:12:22.390 --> 00:12:25.050
structure, and industry expertise.

00:12:26.150 --> 00:12:30.570
Dallas College can provide the platform,<br/>student access, and institutional support.

00:12:31.570 --> 00:12:34.490
This can be structured as<br/>a certification program,

00:12:34.950 --> 00:12:38.750
a continuing education offering,<br/>or workforce training partnership.

00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:41.870
We are flexible, but the goal is the same.

00:12:41.870 --> 00:12:44.950
To create pipelines of<br/>licensed skilled professionals

00:12:44.950 --> 00:12:48.290
entering the workforce quickly and fast.

00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:52.190
In closing, this is more than a program.

00:12:52.410 --> 00:12:57.110
It's an opportunity to modernize<br/>the beauty industry education,

00:12:57.490 --> 00:12:58.950
create faster career pathways,

00:12:59.270 --> 00:13:02.470
and empower the students with some<br/>real income-producing skills.

00:13:03.210 --> 00:13:07.050
Key Academy is ready to partner with Dallas<br/>College to bring the vision forward.

00:13:08.070 --> 00:13:08.870
Thank you.

00:13:08.970 --> 00:13:09.510
Thank you.

00:13:09.510 --> 00:13:11.250
Thank you. Well done.

00:13:17.690 --> 00:13:18.730
That's it.

00:13:18.929 --> 00:13:21.350
Dr. Lonon, you have some special<br/>guests you'd like to introduce.

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:24.610
Yeah, Mr. Chair,<br/>a couple of special presentations.

00:13:24.750 --> 00:13:27.410
I'd like to ask Ahava Silky-Jones<br/>to come to the podium,

00:13:27.910 --> 00:13:30.130
who will start by sharing a<br/>little bit about our

00:13:30.130 --> 00:13:32.330
League of Innovation visual and<br/>literary art winners.

00:13:33.630 --> 00:13:35.910
Thank you very much. Good afternoon.

00:13:37.410 --> 00:13:37.970
There we go.

00:13:38.650 --> 00:13:40.929
Today we are going to celebrate<br/>our League for Innovation

00:13:40.929 --> 00:13:43.809
winners for both our literary<br/>and visual arts.

00:13:44.230 --> 00:13:47.090
Each year,<br/>Dallas College visual arts faculty selects

00:13:47.090 --> 00:13:50.070
a group of ten outstanding student artworks.

00:13:50.070 --> 00:13:54.370
We show these students'<br/>work at the Bill J. Priest Center.

00:13:54.850 --> 00:13:57.150
It just came down last week,<br/>if you missed it,

00:13:57.150 --> 00:14:00.450
but we have some incredible<br/>photos capturing the

00:14:00.450 --> 00:14:01.990
work up on the screen for you.

00:14:01.990 --> 00:14:06.190
It features approximately 70 student<br/>works across disciplines,

00:14:06.330 --> 00:14:08.950
media, techniques,<br/>and creative perspectives.

00:14:09.570 --> 00:14:14.170
Jurors from major museums, galleries,<br/>and arts institutions review this exhibition

00:14:14.170 --> 00:14:18.970
and select the top five student winners to<br/>go on to the international competition,

00:14:19.010 --> 00:14:21.230
which we hope to find out about soon.

00:14:21.810 --> 00:14:25.950
I'd now like to invite Ben Statzer,<br/>Dallas College faculty, to the podium

00:14:25.950 --> 00:14:28.290
to introduce our visual arts winner.

00:14:28.290 --> 00:14:32.050
Ben is a ceramic artist living<br/>and working in Dallas.

00:14:32.270 --> 00:14:34.790
He earned his MFA from the<br/>University of North Texas,

00:14:34.830 --> 00:14:37.210
where he also started his teaching career.

00:14:37.670 --> 00:14:42.870
Ben has taught ceramics at TCC,<br/>Cedar Valley, Eastfield, Brook haven,

00:14:42.890 --> 00:14:46.480
and is now a full-time<br/>faculty member at El Centro.

00:14:47.570 --> 00:14:50.430
Focusing on program growth<br/>and student success,

00:14:50.670 --> 00:14:52.950
Ben spends his energy<br/>creating an environment

00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:57.210
where students are eager to explore,<br/>learn, and engage with the community.

00:14:57.210 --> 00:14:59.570
I will add that if you<br/>have not had the opportunity

00:14:59.570 --> 00:15:02.130
to stop by the Ceramic Studio at El Centro,

00:15:02.170 --> 00:15:05.270
it is always very lively,<br/>and he will invite you to come

00:15:05.270 --> 00:15:06.630
make art with his students.

00:15:06.850 --> 00:15:09.390
Please join me in welcoming<br/>Ben to the podium.

00:15:14.920 --> 00:15:17.660
Good afternoon. Chancellor Lonon,<br/>Chair, Mayor,

00:15:17.820 --> 00:15:20.360
and Board of Trustees, thank you for coming.

00:15:20.440 --> 00:15:23.160
Today I have the pleasure of introducing<br/>one of my amazing students,

00:15:23.460 --> 00:15:24.420
Lolita Hidyeva.

00:15:24.940 --> 00:15:27.460
Lolita is an international<br/>student from Kazakhstan

00:15:27.460 --> 00:15:30.380
currently studying at El Centro,<br/>studying art.

00:15:31.000 --> 00:15:33.060
She has been recognized for<br/>her work many times,

00:15:33.140 --> 00:15:35.260
including awards in the<br/>Founder's Foyer Competition,

00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:38.080
League for Innovation,<br/>the Student Art Exhibition,

00:15:38.220 --> 00:15:40.640
the Fordham Jones Award,<br/>the Chancellor's Art Competition,

00:15:40.640 --> 00:15:43.140
and is currently one of<br/>two Dallas College students

00:15:43.140 --> 00:15:46.080
participating in the Hilton<br/>Anatole Artist Residency.

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:50.560
Lolita's academic excellence and drive<br/>in our art programming

00:15:50.560 --> 00:15:53.180
has made a positive impact<br/>on her instructors,

00:15:53.380 --> 00:15:54.140
her studio mates,

00:15:54.140 --> 00:15:58.400
and our program as a whole.<br/>She's a leader and a joy to be around.

00:15:59.180 --> 00:16:01.920
She has been a pleasure to have in<br/>my class over this past semester,

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:05.300
and the El Centro art faculty<br/>are so excited to see

00:16:05.300 --> 00:16:07.700
what her talent and dedication<br/>will take to it.

00:16:07.840 --> 00:16:18.880
Thank you. Good afternoon.<br/>My name is Lolita.

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:23.420
Dallas College opened up so<br/>many doors for me,

00:16:23.420 --> 00:16:27.400
especially being an international student,<br/>I'm having different and new

00:16:27.400 --> 00:16:28.580
for me experiences.

00:16:29.240 --> 00:16:31.800
I've always dreamed of<br/>getting education abroad

00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:34.300
and become an international artist,

00:16:34.460 --> 00:16:37.100
travel, collaborate,<br/>and keep growing through every

00:16:37.100 --> 00:16:38.960
experience and every person I encounter.

00:16:39.460 --> 00:16:43.020
And Dallas College has taken a<br/>big part in this journey.

00:16:43.820 --> 00:16:47.600
I've participated in many art contests,<br/>won several awards,

00:16:47.740 --> 00:16:52.480
and in this semester I got accepted<br/>into my first art residency.

00:16:52.480 --> 00:16:58.340
One of the biggest achievements I'm proud of<br/>was first ever Chancellor's Art Competition,

00:16:59.120 --> 00:17:03.560
where my artwork became one of<br/>the Dallas permanent collection,

00:17:03.700 --> 00:17:04.940
which I'm so honored.

00:17:05.780 --> 00:17:09.859
I have big ambitions and plans<br/>to move forward with art.

00:17:10.440 --> 00:17:12.300
I'm seeking opportunities to<br/>get a scholarship

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:14.300
and get into an MPA program

00:17:14.300 --> 00:17:18.980
to fully integrate my art studies into my<br/>career and my personal art experience.

00:17:18.980 --> 00:17:26.180
I want to become an art restorer,<br/>working at conservation and leaving my

00:17:26.180 --> 00:17:28.600
own mark on art history.

00:17:30.080 --> 00:17:33.440
Art opportunities matter because they<br/>give you a foundation.

00:17:33.859 --> 00:17:37.080
Participation is everything. Showing up,<br/>getting involved,

00:17:37.180 --> 00:17:38.380
saying yes to opportunities,

00:17:38.600 --> 00:17:41.820
that's how you build your portfolio,<br/>make connections.

00:17:42.240 --> 00:17:46.440
Every project, every performance,<br/>every collaboration is a step

00:17:46.440 --> 00:17:47.660
towards your future.

00:17:47.660 --> 00:17:49.260
Thank you.

00:17:55.119 --> 00:17:57.560
Thank you, Lolita, and congratulations.

00:17:58.340 --> 00:18:00.640
For the League of<br/>Innovation Literary Awards,

00:18:00.760 --> 00:18:02.900
we have four entries from each campus

00:18:02.900 --> 00:18:05.800
that represent the first place<br/>winners in each category.

00:18:06.260 --> 00:18:08.440
That makes seven entries<br/>competing for first,

00:18:08.440 --> 00:18:11.080
second,<br/>and third place, Dallas College wide.

00:18:11.500 --> 00:18:14.220
The first place winners advance<br/>to the national competition,

00:18:14.400 --> 00:18:16.240
where the winners will be<br/>announced this summer.

00:18:16.359 --> 00:18:18.660
So hopefully we'll have some great news<br/>for you in the fall.

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:23.340
It's my pleasure now to introduce<br/>Professor Rebecca Rios-Harris.

00:18:23.540 --> 00:18:26.180
Rebecca has been the Dallas College League<br/>for Innovation Literary

00:18:26.180 --> 00:18:27.180
Competition Coordinator

00:18:27.180 --> 00:18:30.260
for over 20 years, so you know Rebecca well.

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:34.420
And she has really identified this<br/>as a calling for her.

00:18:34.520 --> 00:18:37.240
She started her journey as<br/>a developmental writing

00:18:37.240 --> 00:18:38.900
adjunct and has been teaching English

00:18:39.180 --> 00:18:43.520
and integrated reading and writing full<br/>time for over 34 years.

00:18:43.940 --> 00:18:47.140
She has been a discipline coordinator and<br/>a leader on numerous teams

00:18:47.140 --> 00:18:49.859
focused on assessment and<br/>improving the English

00:18:49.859 --> 00:18:52.119
and integrated reading and<br/>writing curriculums

00:18:52.119 --> 00:18:55.500
across Dallas College,<br/>in addition to serving as

00:18:55.500 --> 00:18:56.900
Phi Theta Kappa advisor.

00:18:57.280 --> 00:18:59.060
Please join me in welcoming Rebecca.

00:19:05.060 --> 00:19:06.980
Thank you, Vice Provost Silky Jones.

00:19:07.900 --> 00:19:10.340
Hello, Chancellor Laughnan, Chair,<br/>Mayor, and Trustees.

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:13.480
It's good to be here.<br/>Always happy to see all of you.

00:19:13.840 --> 00:19:18.900
But I'm even more excited to introduce<br/>literary competitors that do really well.

00:19:18.900 --> 00:19:22.460
All of our students are so awesome.<br/>It's sad we can't pick four or

00:19:22.460 --> 00:19:24.080
five first-place winners every time.

00:19:24.780 --> 00:19:28.020
But this year's host for the<br/>League for Innovation Literary Competition

00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:31.220
is Anna Rundell Community<br/>College in Maryland.

00:19:31.580 --> 00:19:35.100
So that's where our first-place winners from<br/>each category got sent to that school.

00:19:36.060 --> 00:19:38.660
And Vice Chancellor... I'm<br/>not Vice Chancellor,

00:19:38.840 --> 00:19:40.119
I'm promoting her.

00:19:40.480 --> 00:19:44.680
Vice Provost Silky Jones said as well that<br/>we will find out this summer.

00:19:44.940 --> 00:19:47.320
I'm eager to hear how well<br/>our first-place winners did.

00:19:47.320 --> 00:19:50.400
This year's theme is called Fisher's.

00:19:50.960 --> 00:19:54.640
And of course, to Fisher,<br/>it's to crack or cleave or divide.

00:19:55.560 --> 00:19:58.420
And Creative Writing explores these cracks,<br/>and that's what our students have

00:19:58.420 --> 00:20:00.880
done outstandingly this year.

00:20:02.020 --> 00:20:06.020
Our contest always begins, as she said,<br/>with campus competitions.

00:20:06.240 --> 00:20:09.920
And each campus coordinator also<br/>becomes our Dallas College

00:20:09.920 --> 00:20:12.440
judges for that level of the competition.

00:20:12.760 --> 00:20:15.260
And I do want to take the<br/>time really quickly to thank

00:20:15.260 --> 00:20:18.500
Aaron Clark from Brook haven,<br/>Laurie Phillips from El Centro,

00:20:19.119 --> 00:20:22.740
Rufel Ramos from Eastfield,<br/>Darius Frishour from Mountain View,

00:20:23.040 --> 00:20:25.940
Brett Bodely from Northlake,<br/>and William Matter from Richland.

00:20:26.220 --> 00:20:29.520
And speaking of Richland,<br/>we had a Richland sweep this year.

00:20:29.880 --> 00:20:34.619
Richland campus had all four first<br/>place winners in the categories.

00:20:34.820 --> 00:20:36.660
So that is commendable.

00:20:37.619 --> 00:20:42.400
I also want to say that Jenna Trong,<br/>she was a first-place winner

00:20:42.400 --> 00:20:43.760
for her personal essay,

00:20:43.760 --> 00:20:46.640
lost in translation,<br/>was supposed to be here,

00:20:46.680 --> 00:20:48.200
and then couldn't make it.

00:20:48.359 --> 00:20:50.280
But she did ask me to say,

00:20:50.500 --> 00:20:55.220
I want to thank Dallas College for providing<br/>me with a strong educational foundation

00:20:55.220 --> 00:20:58.119
and highly beneficial student<br/>centered resources.

00:20:58.619 --> 00:21:00.580
Further, I want to thank<br/>my English professor,

00:21:00.600 --> 00:21:01.580
Dr. William Matter,

00:21:01.920 --> 00:21:04.660
for encouraging me to submit<br/>my essay for consideration

00:21:04.660 --> 00:21:07.100
in the League for<br/>Innovation Literary Contest.

00:21:07.520 --> 00:21:10.260
The support and opportunities provided<br/>by Dallas College

00:21:10.260 --> 00:21:11.880
have helped to shape my future.

00:21:11.880 --> 00:21:13.660
And that's wonderful.

00:21:14.960 --> 00:21:20.700
Now, Ngoc Phung Cham Chan is a<br/>biology major at Dallas College.

00:21:20.980 --> 00:21:23.440
She is also an international<br/>student and hopes to

00:21:23.440 --> 00:21:25.800
become a hospital pharmacist in the future.

00:21:26.380 --> 00:21:30.060
Outside of school, she enjoys writing,<br/>spending time with friends,

00:21:30.260 --> 00:21:35.100
and having relaxing days where she explores<br/>cafes or walks around the city.

00:21:35.820 --> 00:21:40.800
I am honored to present Richland campus<br/>student Ngoc Phung Cham Chan,

00:21:40.800 --> 00:21:43.980
our Dallas College first-place<br/>winner for her one

00:21:43.980 --> 00:21:46.880
act play titled Two Versions of Me.

00:21:58.230 --> 00:21:59.710
Good afternoon, everyone.

00:22:00.830 --> 00:22:03.670
Thank you for giving me the<br/>opportunity to speak today.

00:22:03.970 --> 00:22:06.670
My name is Ngoc Phung Cham Chan,<br/>and I am an international

00:22:06.670 --> 00:22:07.830
student at Dallas College.

00:22:09.330 --> 00:22:11.850
Because English is not my first language,

00:22:12.109 --> 00:22:14.410
so that's why during the first<br/>time I came here,

00:22:14.550 --> 00:22:17.490
I had many trouble with studying English.

00:22:18.250 --> 00:22:24.369
I often ask a lot about writing,<br/>but I know I think my

00:22:24.369 --> 00:22:25.730
idea is good for share.

00:22:26.869 --> 00:22:29.630
Because of that,<br/>winning the first place in literary

00:22:29.630 --> 00:22:31.470
content has meant a lot to me.

00:22:31.690 --> 00:22:34.650
It has made me more confident<br/>in myself and reminded

00:22:34.650 --> 00:22:37.570
me that my voice and my experience matter.

00:22:38.050 --> 00:22:41.570
I am really grateful to<br/>my professor at Dallas

00:22:41.570 --> 00:22:45.770
College for creating an<br/>environment for students

00:22:45.770 --> 00:22:49.750
who support and encourage to grow up.

00:22:50.609 --> 00:22:56.150
And this experience has motivated<br/>me to keep moving,

00:22:56.630 --> 00:23:00.510
improve my writing skills and<br/>challenge in my future.

00:23:01.290 --> 00:23:02.290
Thank you for listening.

00:23:12.190 --> 00:23:15.330
Great. Thank you all for being here.<br/>Come on up and we'll get a photo.

00:24:29.940 --> 00:24:32.560
Because the next group is very subtle.

00:24:34.900 --> 00:24:39.960
And so some of you were able to go<br/>to the Future of Fashion Design Showcase.

00:24:40.900 --> 00:24:43.359
And so I'd like to have to<br/>share a little bit more detail.

00:24:44.180 --> 00:24:49.280
Yes, thank you so much to so many of you<br/>that supported us that evening

00:24:49.280 --> 00:24:50.420
of our fashion show.

00:24:50.640 --> 00:24:54.500
And if you weren't able to be there,<br/>I heard a lot of wonderful feedback.

00:24:54.619 --> 00:24:55.940
So thank you for that.

00:24:56.700 --> 00:25:00.840
The fashion show at Dallas College is<br/>a culminating event for Arts Month.

00:25:00.840 --> 00:25:05.359
Throughout the course of Arts Month,<br/>we produced 66 events in 30 days,

00:25:05.660 --> 00:25:07.619
16 of which were in the community.

00:25:07.980 --> 00:25:13.140
We had over a thousand attendees at<br/>our performance events and 757,

00:25:13.160 --> 00:25:13.920
who's counting,

00:25:14.280 --> 00:25:18.000
at our gallery receptions and<br/>art collection tours.

00:25:18.460 --> 00:25:22.220
The fashion show brought together an<br/>extraordinary group of partners,

00:25:22.619 --> 00:25:26.400
led by our fashion design faculty,<br/>department chair and students

00:25:26.400 --> 00:25:27.520
with the vision,

00:25:27.520 --> 00:25:31.140
our live events and gallery team<br/>as our event management,

00:25:31.440 --> 00:25:34.080
communications, marketing and<br/>our foundation,

00:25:34.780 --> 00:25:38.840
events team, who helped us activate<br/>our VIP experience and funding.

00:25:39.440 --> 00:25:42.300
We had over 14 press<br/>releases throughout the month,

00:25:42.600 --> 00:25:43.780
coverage and patron magazine,

00:25:44.020 --> 00:25:47.540
Glass Tire, Dallas Morning News,<br/>a Fox Four broadcast feature,

00:25:48.119 --> 00:25:52.820
16 digital billboards across DFW,<br/>and tens of thousands of

00:25:52.820 --> 00:25:53.880
social media impressions.

00:25:53.880 --> 00:25:57.680
So really feeling the energy and love<br/>for the School of Creative Arts,

00:25:57.920 --> 00:25:59.260
Entertainment and Design.

00:25:59.320 --> 00:26:03.359
And now you will feel the energy and<br/>love of our fashion design program.

00:26:03.740 --> 00:26:06.060
I would like to personally<br/>invite Emanuel Tobias

00:26:06.060 --> 00:26:07.960
to the stage in just a moment.

00:26:08.119 --> 00:26:11.580
Emanuel is a fashion educator,<br/>creative producer and mentor,

00:26:12.040 --> 00:26:14.340
dedicated to developing the<br/>next generation of

00:26:14.340 --> 00:26:16.400
industry talent through<br/>innovative programming,

00:26:16.780 --> 00:26:18.960
event production and industry collaboration.

00:26:18.960 --> 00:26:22.900
As the lead behind the annual<br/>Future of Fashion Showcase,

00:26:22.920 --> 00:26:25.560
he has helped connect students<br/>with professional designers,

00:26:25.859 --> 00:26:27.080
buyers and media opportunities.

00:26:27.900 --> 00:26:30.540
While championing student success<br/>and creative excellence,

00:26:30.880 --> 00:26:34.680
he is also a Dallas College<br/>alum of our fashion program.

00:26:35.380 --> 00:26:38.660
And you can see the pictures<br/>speak for themselves about

00:26:38.660 --> 00:26:41.900
the extraordinary event that he<br/>put together this year.

00:26:42.000 --> 00:26:45.119
Please join me in welcoming<br/>Emanuel to the stage.

00:26:49.140 --> 00:26:51.780
Hello, everyone. Good afternoon,<br/>Chair Meyer,

00:26:51.980 --> 00:26:54.840
Chancellor Lonon and Dallas College<br/>Board of Trustees.

00:26:55.560 --> 00:27:00.340
Thank you for having us again and having our<br/>little fashion program here year after year.

00:27:00.420 --> 00:27:05.240
And we're here to celebrate the achievements<br/>that we've displayed throughout the year.

00:27:05.460 --> 00:27:08.180
And thank you to those of you<br/>who attended our show this year.

00:27:09.140 --> 00:27:12.540
It is my honor to introduce<br/>two very special students who

00:27:12.540 --> 00:27:14.900
have been an incredible part<br/>of our fashion program.

00:27:14.900 --> 00:27:17.560
Carlos Cardona and Christian Henderson.

00:27:18.540 --> 00:27:22.700
In education, we often celebrate talent,<br/>creativity and achievement.

00:27:23.380 --> 00:27:26.140
And both of these young men<br/>certainly carry these things.

00:27:26.600 --> 00:27:29.900
But what makes them truly<br/>special is everything

00:27:29.900 --> 00:27:31.460
that they do behind the scenes.

00:27:32.780 --> 00:27:38.220
I've had the honor to give these<br/>young men a cute little superlative.

00:27:38.220 --> 00:27:41.320
And if I would give them that,<br/>I would call them, you good,

00:27:41.320 --> 00:27:45.200
Mr. Tobias, for always showing up<br/>when it mattered the most,

00:27:45.380 --> 00:27:48.400
especially during the long nights,<br/>stressful production days,

00:27:48.980 --> 00:27:51.180
chaotic pop-up building sessions,

00:27:51.780 --> 00:27:54.859
lifting heavy set pieces or<br/>randomly appearing to give

00:27:54.859 --> 00:27:57.000
me a Coke Zero or a Red Bull.

00:27:58.200 --> 00:28:00.300
So more than helpers,<br/>they have been a constant

00:28:00.300 --> 00:28:04.000
source of encouragement,<br/>support and reliability,

00:28:04.000 --> 00:28:08.359
not only for their classmates,<br/>but for me personally throughout the year.

00:28:09.160 --> 00:28:11.880
Christian has achieved<br/>incredible recognition

00:28:11.880 --> 00:28:14.740
this year as a<br/>finalist for Pierre Cardin

00:28:14.740 --> 00:28:16.100
Young Designers Award,

00:28:16.340 --> 00:28:21.900
where he was selected among only 20 students<br/>nationwide out of thousands of applicants

00:28:21.900 --> 00:28:27.040
to participate in an exclusive workshop<br/>experience with the Parisian Couture

00:28:27.040 --> 00:28:29.820
House here in Dallas and<br/>their special design team.

00:28:29.820 --> 00:28:34.460
He was also recognized as a finalist by<br/>Fashion Group International in

00:28:34.460 --> 00:28:35.119
the denim category

00:28:35.440 --> 00:28:40.040
and was also named our 2026 Future<br/>of Fashion Best of Show winner.

00:28:41.160 --> 00:28:43.140
Carlos, the designer of the<br/>award-winning look

00:28:43.140 --> 00:28:44.780
that I am proudly wearing today,

00:28:45.400 --> 00:28:50.100
was honored as our 2026 Future<br/>of Fashion Collections Design winner.

00:28:50.820 --> 00:28:54.260
His creativity,<br/>craftsmanship and artistic vision have made

00:28:54.260 --> 00:28:56.420
a lasting impression on our program.

00:28:56.420 --> 00:29:01.060
And everyone who has encountered his work,<br/>including K.J. Moody. He was also

00:29:01.060 --> 00:29:02.040
one of our guest judges.

00:29:02.160 --> 00:29:05.480
He was a celebrity stylist for Beyoncé,<br/>the Renaissance Tour,

00:29:06.000 --> 00:29:08.460
Normani and several other<br/>A-list celebrities.

00:29:09.320 --> 00:29:13.620
And I also want to recognize Carlos'<br/>extraordinary resilience and strength

00:29:13.620 --> 00:29:14.200
this year.

00:29:14.580 --> 00:29:17.360
After experiencing the heartbreaking loss<br/>of his sister,

00:29:17.820 --> 00:29:20.040
he still showed up,<br/>completed his collection,

00:29:20.560 --> 00:29:23.340
supported those around him and<br/>persevered with grace

00:29:23.340 --> 00:29:26.160
and determination without making<br/>any excuses.

00:29:26.160 --> 00:29:29.660
That level of character is<br/>truly special and I

00:29:29.660 --> 00:29:32.440
believe he deserves to be honored today.

00:29:33.280 --> 00:29:35.680
It is truly an honor to<br/>recognize both of them.

00:29:36.040 --> 00:29:39.520
And I cannot wait to see the impact that<br/>they continue to make in

00:29:39.520 --> 00:29:41.940
our fashion industry,<br/>the community and beyond.

00:29:42.640 --> 00:29:43.680
Thank you, Carlos.

00:29:52.140 --> 00:29:55.020
Sorry if I mispronounced these names,<br/>but I want to start off

00:29:55.020 --> 00:29:57.300
by thanking Chair and Mayor,

00:29:57.300 --> 00:29:59.960
Chancellor Lonon and the Dallas College<br/>of Board of Trustees

00:29:59.960 --> 00:30:01.700
for giving me the ability<br/>to speak here today.

00:30:03.780 --> 00:30:07.380
I just want to start off by saying that<br/>Dallas College has supported me

00:30:07.380 --> 00:30:08.340
through my journey.

00:30:10.860 --> 00:30:14.700
By giving me the safe space<br/>to work at the school,

00:30:15.400 --> 00:30:20.600
to give me many,<br/>many chances to kind of take the ideas

00:30:20.600 --> 00:30:23.040
I have and put them out into the real world.

00:30:23.040 --> 00:30:27.000
But also having an amazing staff,<br/>always ready.

00:30:27.300 --> 00:30:33.280
My professors always started to support me<br/>and definitely backed me up.

00:30:34.140 --> 00:30:37.880
Without them, I don't know if I<br/>would have gotten this far.

00:30:38.600 --> 00:30:41.360
At some point I wanted to actually quit.

00:30:42.440 --> 00:30:47.920
But they, through time and effort,<br/>definitely gave me the advice and I stayed

00:30:47.920 --> 00:30:49.560
and I kept going at it.

00:30:49.560 --> 00:30:50.900
And well, I won.

00:30:56.440 --> 00:31:00.060
But Dallas College has been supporting each<br/>one of us by giving us

00:31:00.060 --> 00:31:03.180
the opportunity to do good for our<br/>community by supplying the resources.

00:31:03.840 --> 00:31:06.480
And that is something I'm<br/>eternally grateful for.

00:31:06.920 --> 00:31:10.860
Every single time I go to campus,<br/>I'm always so happy that,

00:31:10.860 --> 00:31:12.840
you know, I stuck with it.

00:31:14.320 --> 00:31:19.000
And yeah, I think about it every day<br/>and I'm eternally grateful to the school.

00:31:19.000 --> 00:31:23.880
I'm most proud of, once again,<br/>my professors. Huge inspiration to me.

00:31:24.340 --> 00:31:26.700
They always put themselves last and always<br/>make sure that the youth

00:31:26.700 --> 00:31:28.180
have a good chance to make it in this world.

00:31:29.180 --> 00:31:34.880
They always put themselves last and<br/>that's something I think of

00:31:34.880 --> 00:31:37.180
so much and I'm so grateful to have them.

00:31:37.320 --> 00:31:42.060
Especially Mr. Tobias, my professor,<br/>was always there to guide me as well.

00:31:42.420 --> 00:31:45.600
Especially through the tough times I<br/>had during finals week.

00:31:46.980 --> 00:31:50.980
I'm also proud of myself and how<br/>far I've gone through my journey,

00:31:51.980 --> 00:31:52.900
skill-wise.

00:31:53.480 --> 00:31:56.660
I had such a difficult time trying to<br/>understand everything and grasp the concept.

00:31:57.480 --> 00:32:02.880
And even my other professor, Ms. Duckworth,<br/>a lovely woman, very talented.

00:32:03.400 --> 00:32:05.620
And she also made sure that<br/>I didn't give up.

00:32:07.300 --> 00:32:11.340
I believe our opportunities at<br/>Dallas College that provides

00:32:11.340 --> 00:32:13.340
are very essential since it<br/>gives students hope.

00:32:13.340 --> 00:32:16.060
We get such a drive and we see just how<br/>far we can go with

00:32:16.060 --> 00:32:17.600
the opportunities at hand.

00:32:18.080 --> 00:32:21.760
It's amazing that we have events<br/>for newcomers and scholarships for

00:32:21.760 --> 00:32:24.280
our hardworking students to continue<br/>working towards their dream.

00:32:24.600 --> 00:32:28.740
Hopefully, our fashion department and our<br/>opportunities can get bigger every

00:32:28.740 --> 00:32:30.780
year so that we can show<br/>the future of fashion.

00:32:31.820 --> 00:32:34.580
Today, I would like to show you<br/>two of my designs that I've

00:32:34.580 --> 00:32:38.380
created out of a set of eight<br/>that I'm very proud of.

00:32:40.600 --> 00:32:44.540
They feature Sashiko hand stitching,<br/>which is a type of hand

00:32:44.540 --> 00:32:48.620
sewing from Japan that<br/>I would like to put into all my work.

00:32:49.000 --> 00:32:53.900
Very extensive hours and hours<br/>of hand sewing.

00:32:55.200 --> 00:33:00.140
So I just hope you guys enjoy it. And yeah,<br/>thank you so much. I appreciate it.

00:33:06.190 --> 00:33:07.310
I've got a question.

00:33:08.930 --> 00:33:12.050
Carlos, I've got a question.<br/>I'm sorry for Carlos.

00:33:13.550 --> 00:33:15.770
So do you do the hand stitching yourself?

00:33:16.370 --> 00:33:20.690
Yes, ma'am. All the outfits,<br/>individual stitches done by hand. Yes,

00:33:20.710 --> 00:33:20.970
ma'am.

00:33:21.290 --> 00:33:24.410
Interesting. And why aren't you wearing<br/>one of your outfits?

00:33:27.810 --> 00:33:31.610
Well, my father does screen printing.<br/>So I did print out a shirt of mine.

00:33:32.930 --> 00:33:35.250
That I printed on the day of the show.

00:33:37.270 --> 00:33:39.770
But I was actually talking about<br/>this earlier in the hallway.

00:33:40.630 --> 00:33:45.710
A lot of the times, as a designer,<br/>you spend so much money that you work so

00:33:45.710 --> 00:33:46.690
hard for to spend on your garments.

00:33:46.890 --> 00:33:48.850
And then you walk in just a<br/>t-shirt and some shorts.

00:33:51.150 --> 00:33:53.950
But yeah, I'm just glad I<br/>got the opportunity to

00:33:53.950 --> 00:33:55.710
do what I can. So I'm eternally grateful.

00:33:55.850 --> 00:33:57.510
And thank you so much for enjoying my work.

00:33:57.590 --> 00:33:59.590
Good work. Good job.

00:34:06.900 --> 00:34:09.600
Hello, everybody. My name<br/>is Christian Henderson.

00:34:09.780 --> 00:34:13.400
I'm a graduate from Ive School, Oxyhatchee.

00:34:14.340 --> 00:34:17.800
I came to El Centro in<br/>2022 to study fashion design.

00:34:18.620 --> 00:34:23.540
And that was me not knowing<br/>how to thread the machine.

00:34:24.000 --> 00:34:27.219
So to go from that to this is<br/>just a testament of the school.

00:34:28.420 --> 00:34:31.120
And I would just like to<br/>talk about our program today.

00:34:31.400 --> 00:34:34.360
So as I try and find words to<br/>describe the El Centro

00:34:34.360 --> 00:34:35.560
fashion design program,

00:34:35.560 --> 00:34:38.360
the first words that come to<br/>my mind is a garden.

00:34:39.780 --> 00:34:45.800
In this garden, fruits are grown of passion,<br/>community, creative expression,

00:34:46.020 --> 00:34:46.680
and identity.

00:34:48.580 --> 00:34:52.700
The sowers of these seeds are professors<br/>who pour their everything into us

00:34:52.700 --> 00:34:55.120
because it's more than just a<br/>job but it's their passion.

00:34:55.940 --> 00:35:00.719
From late nights to answering any<br/>questions that we may have

00:35:00.719 --> 00:35:04.219
to helping us and guiding us just<br/>every step of the way.

00:35:05.060 --> 00:35:07.260
They are there with us<br/>throughout our whole creative

00:35:07.260 --> 00:35:09.600
process constantly pushing us to be better.

00:35:10.540 --> 00:35:13.940
And it really just helps when you're<br/>feeling like you're in a corner

00:35:13.940 --> 00:35:16.960
or you can't get past this<br/>obstacle or this problem

00:35:16.960 --> 00:35:19.280
or you don't have the<br/>confidence to move forward.

00:35:19.760 --> 00:35:22.080
Just them there basically hand<br/>in hand walking

00:35:22.080 --> 00:35:24.020
with you through the whole process.

00:35:24.420 --> 00:35:27.040
And like I said,<br/>I've been here for four years and

00:35:27.040 --> 00:35:28.060
it's been on my mind,

00:35:28.140 --> 00:35:30.760
like, am I taking too long?<br/>But they sat down with me and like,

00:35:30.820 --> 00:35:31.880
no, just take your time.

00:35:33.219 --> 00:35:37.739
I would also like to talk about how<br/>they helped me with my journey.

00:35:37.980 --> 00:35:42.380
I suffer from a visual<br/>impairment called nystagmus,

00:35:42.980 --> 00:35:45.140
which basically makes my eyes<br/>dance around so I

00:35:45.140 --> 00:35:47.560
can't focus or my sight is impaired.

00:35:48.880 --> 00:35:52.300
And as you can tell,<br/>I'm wearing my headgear today

00:35:52.300 --> 00:35:55.120
and usually I feel embarrassed<br/>about wearing it,

00:35:55.239 --> 00:35:58.920
but my professors, classmates,<br/>and colleagues all have given

00:35:58.920 --> 00:35:59.680
me the confidence

00:35:59.680 --> 00:36:04.000
to kind of embrace that part of me as<br/>like a gift and not a curse.

00:36:05.960 --> 00:36:09.400
So instead of running away from it,<br/>they told me to face it forward

00:36:09.400 --> 00:36:14.360
and keep pushing myself to be<br/>a better version of myself.

00:36:15.180 --> 00:36:19.620
So I want to say thank you on behalf of<br/>all the students from the

00:36:19.620 --> 00:36:20.820
Future of Fashion program.

00:36:20.900 --> 00:36:24.520
And I would love to showcase two<br/>of my designs from my collection.

00:36:24.520 --> 00:36:28.080
I'm wearing one and then my classmate<br/>Joshua is wearing one too.

00:36:48.200 --> 00:36:50.980
I've also got a comment for you.

00:36:51.300 --> 00:36:54.780
So at the fashion show,<br/>I sat across from your

00:36:54.780 --> 00:36:55.719
parents on the runway.

00:36:56.040 --> 00:36:57.880
They are so proud of you.

00:36:58.020 --> 00:37:01.739
It was so wonderful to see how proud<br/>and beaming they were that night

00:37:01.739 --> 00:37:04.540
when you came out and they<br/>were taking all those pictures.

00:37:04.540 --> 00:37:07.760
And in terms of your headgear,<br/>I thought that was part

00:37:07.760 --> 00:37:08.980
of your fashion look.

00:37:09.280 --> 00:37:11.140
It looks good. Thank you.

00:37:11.140 --> 00:37:12.800
So don't be shy about wearing it.

00:37:12.960 --> 00:37:17.760
Yeah, so it's taken me a while to<br/>have the confidence to even wear it,

00:37:17.780 --> 00:37:20.660
especially in public. Even now,<br/>it's a little nerve-wrecking,

00:37:21.340 --> 00:37:23.420
but it's just a part of who<br/>I am. You look great.

00:37:23.920 --> 00:37:26.880
And just with my parents,<br/>the amount of sacrifice they put in,

00:37:27.160 --> 00:37:31.400
it was great for me to see<br/>them having fun and being proud.

00:37:32.860 --> 00:37:33.540
Thank you.

00:37:39.719 --> 00:37:42.700
Well, thank you all for representing<br/>Dallas College so well.

00:37:42.760 --> 00:37:46.239
Mr. Tobias, thank you, as always,<br/>for all you do to support our students.

00:37:46.719 --> 00:37:48.380
Thank you for being here.<br/>If you want to come up,

00:37:48.480 --> 00:37:49.520
I'd love to get a photo.

00:39:22.380 --> 00:39:24.860
Oh, thank you.

00:39:25.000 --> 00:39:26.560
Thank you so much for coming.

00:39:31.930 --> 00:39:34.610
Yeah, because it's in line with this.

00:39:35.950 --> 00:39:38.710
About the fashion show. So<br/>one of the students

00:39:38.710 --> 00:39:40.190
that thinks she was at the end,

00:39:41.150 --> 00:39:45.110
she accessorized her fashions<br/>with jewelry from

00:39:45.110 --> 00:39:46.890
a place where I shopped.

00:39:46.950 --> 00:39:49.950
And as a matter of fact,<br/>one of the necklaces that one of her models

00:39:49.950 --> 00:39:51.450
had on is a necklace I have.

00:39:52.250 --> 00:39:55.850
And the shop, it's UU Cultural Shop.<br/>It's one of our entrepreneurs

00:39:55.850 --> 00:39:57.190
and chamber board members.

00:39:57.250 --> 00:40:00.890
So it was really neat to see that and the<br/>touch she provided to her

00:40:00.890 --> 00:40:03.090
fashions with those accessories,<br/>the jewelry.

00:40:03.090 --> 00:40:04.930
Perfect. Thank you.

00:40:09.060 --> 00:40:14.260
So, Mr. Chair,<br/>I do want to also mention that Dallas

00:40:14.260 --> 00:40:18.600
College was recently named an Achieving<br/>the Dream Leader College.

00:40:19.080 --> 00:40:24.460
This is a national recognition that is<br/>for colleges that deliver sustained,

00:40:24.460 --> 00:40:28.140
measurable gains and student outcomes<br/>while advancing student

00:40:28.140 --> 00:40:30.760
success and economic mobility<br/>in their communities.

00:40:31.500 --> 00:40:34.080
Institutions earning this honor<br/>demonstrate strong

00:40:34.080 --> 00:40:38.160
completion and retention rates,<br/>a culture of data informed decision making,

00:40:38.620 --> 00:40:40.540
and proven strategies that<br/>close achievement gaps.

00:40:40.739 --> 00:40:45.180
This marks the first time that Dallas<br/>College has received this distinction.

00:40:45.600 --> 00:40:49.300
This award is a powerful validation of the<br/>college's transformation and commitment

00:40:49.300 --> 00:40:50.400
to student success.

00:40:50.820 --> 00:40:54.120
So just for the second time,<br/>I want to mention and acknowledge Dr.

00:40:54.320 --> 00:40:58.420
Floyd and Dr. Joseph and their<br/>teams for this designation.

00:40:58.420 --> 00:41:00.000
Thank you.

00:41:02.739 --> 00:41:04.380
And you don't have to get a picture with us.

00:41:05.320 --> 00:41:13.540
All right. That's presentations. Chancellor,<br/>do you have any announcements?

00:41:14.020 --> 00:41:18.140
Just one announcement. If you're unaware,<br/>graduation starts this week.

00:41:18.800 --> 00:41:23.060
So six commencement exercises,<br/>thousands of students over a

00:41:23.060 --> 00:41:26.520
three day period,<br/>the culmination of the work of every

00:41:26.520 --> 00:41:28.040
member of the Dallas College team.

00:41:28.040 --> 00:41:32.520
As we get to be a part of the<br/>students journey as they cross that stage,

00:41:32.520 --> 00:41:36.940
see the excitement on their faces,<br/>see the excitement of their families and

00:41:36.940 --> 00:41:39.500
their friends that are there,<br/>gathered there.

00:41:39.640 --> 00:41:43.100
So thank you to everyone that<br/>every day has helped

00:41:43.100 --> 00:41:45.120
support these students get to<br/>where they are.

00:41:45.460 --> 00:41:50.360
Thank you to our events team for putting on<br/>this major production over that

00:41:50.360 --> 00:41:51.260
three day period.

00:41:51.980 --> 00:41:57.440
And thank you to the volunteers because<br/>we have numerous volunteers that support

00:41:57.440 --> 00:42:01.219
this so we can support thousands of<br/>students over those three days.

00:42:01.420 --> 00:42:03.760
So I look forward to seeing you all there.

00:42:05.640 --> 00:42:06.920
Any other trustees?

00:42:07.520 --> 00:42:14.060
I do. I would like to take this<br/>time to kind of share with

00:42:14.060 --> 00:42:18.500
you that on May the 30th on<br/>a Saturday from 10 a.m.

00:42:18.500 --> 00:42:24.480
until 2 p.m., we're going to hold an event.

00:42:24.640 --> 00:42:28.719
It's going to be and I've got some<br/>brochures that will be

00:42:28.719 --> 00:42:30.900
disseminated countywide.

00:42:31.580 --> 00:42:35.300
But basically what we're trying to<br/>do is is showcase

00:42:35.300 --> 00:42:38.700
Dallas College in a regional<br/>area of the county.

00:42:38.700 --> 00:42:42.780
So this is basically focusing<br/>on Southwest Dallas County,

00:42:43.420 --> 00:42:48.700
the territory that I represent and in<br/>my position as a trustee.

00:42:50.020 --> 00:42:52.820
What I'm really wanting to do<br/>and I've asked the

00:42:52.820 --> 00:42:56.200
event team and the whole<br/>team to put together

00:42:56.200 --> 00:43:03.320
is that I want us to be able to<br/>offer some food and drink and family time.

00:43:03.320 --> 00:43:08.940
Because the way I see an event like this,<br/>it's it's for that father who might

00:43:08.940 --> 00:43:10.120
want to be up skilled.

00:43:10.520 --> 00:43:15.380
It's for that father or mother who lost her<br/>job that maybe they're needing a new job.

00:43:15.700 --> 00:43:19.100
So they need some credentials.<br/>They need another start in life.

00:43:19.460 --> 00:43:25.000
And also the dual credit programs,<br/>the programs that we offer and

00:43:25.000 --> 00:43:27.900
then those who are<br/>just wanting to start college

00:43:27.900 --> 00:43:29.040
for the first time.

00:43:29.380 --> 00:43:31.440
So we're making it a family affair.

00:43:31.440 --> 00:43:36.160
We're blessed to have such a great<br/>facility at the shops of Redbird,

00:43:36.580 --> 00:43:38.440
the old what's known as Redbird Mall.

00:43:38.940 --> 00:43:45.000
It has been transformed. UT Southwestern,<br/>Parkland, Texas Workforce Commission.

00:43:45.600 --> 00:43:49.140
There's just some major,<br/>major activities that occur there

00:43:49.140 --> 00:43:50.400
on a daily basis.

00:43:51.080 --> 00:43:54.280
And I just want to invite<br/>everyone to come out.

00:43:54.920 --> 00:43:59.320
I'm going to go address each one of<br/>the city councils in those cities.

00:43:59.320 --> 00:44:03.580
I go tonight to Cedar Hill<br/>and I'll be presenting to

00:44:03.580 --> 00:44:06.580
the city council what we're<br/>offering for their community.

00:44:07.640 --> 00:44:11.160
And we're going to be leaving<br/>these brochures at all

00:44:11.160 --> 00:44:14.000
of the outreach ministries that<br/>are in the county.

00:44:14.340 --> 00:44:19.060
People who are there getting food and rent<br/>of substance that don't have a job.

00:44:19.120 --> 00:44:21.380
So why wouldn't that be a perfect place?

00:44:21.780 --> 00:44:24.960
So I'm just asking everybody who<br/>would like to come

00:44:24.960 --> 00:44:28.380
and see a fantastic event to come out.

00:44:28.380 --> 00:44:32.580
We're going to have all the<br/>colleges. We'll have everyone there.

00:44:32.620 --> 00:44:35.540
Registrar is going to be there.<br/>We're going to have the

00:44:35.540 --> 00:44:37.239
financial aid group there.

00:44:37.680 --> 00:44:42.320
And so everything that we have to offer<br/>is going to be on showcase.

00:44:42.719 --> 00:44:47.380
And we feel this is going to be<br/>a person to person type marketing effort

00:44:47.380 --> 00:44:51.340
that I believe that will<br/>ultimately be effective

00:44:51.340 --> 00:44:53.120
in all segments of the county.

00:44:53.440 --> 00:44:55.820
But we're looking forward to it.

00:44:55.820 --> 00:44:59.520
And I think that that event team they<br/>referred to has done a fabulous job.

00:44:59.960 --> 00:45:02.920
They work hard. We've been working<br/>on this probably for six

00:45:02.920 --> 00:45:06.540
or seven months just trying<br/>to figure this out.

00:45:06.739 --> 00:45:13.620
And so I just encourage everyone to come<br/>in and we're doing email blasts

00:45:13.620 --> 00:45:17.860
to all the school districts in that<br/>area to get the people out.

00:45:18.219 --> 00:45:20.860
So I invite everyone to come in.

00:45:20.860 --> 00:45:23.140
Everybody come have a good time.

00:45:23.400 --> 00:45:24.980
I'm cooking lunch today.

00:45:29.000 --> 00:45:31.280
So I didn't think I was going to<br/>make it to four o'clock,

00:45:31.340 --> 00:45:32.780
but I drank a cup of coffee.

00:45:33.200 --> 00:45:37.120
It kind of woke me up. Anyway,<br/>so some of the things I

00:45:37.120 --> 00:45:37.880
was going to announce.

00:45:39.040 --> 00:45:41.800
I had planned to originally announce here.<br/>I announced over there because

00:45:41.800 --> 00:45:42.920
I didn't know if I was going to make it.

00:45:42.920 --> 00:45:50.480
But another thing. So last Friday,<br/>I was at the location of Amance.

00:45:50.600 --> 00:45:52.739
That's an early childhood program.

00:45:53.340 --> 00:45:56.560
They focus on teaching the parents how<br/>to be the first teacher.

00:45:57.120 --> 00:46:00.280
And they have very good outcomes in<br/>terms of the students of

00:46:00.280 --> 00:46:12.400
those parents that actually when they<br/>come out of high school,

00:46:12.400 --> 00:46:18.320
And two years ago, in Mexico,<br/>El Día del Niño was

00:46:18.320 --> 00:46:20.000
celebrated on April 30th.

00:46:20.000 --> 00:46:24.460
And two years ago,<br/>I facilitated for them to have that

00:46:24.460 --> 00:46:25.719
celebration at the West Center.

00:46:26.520 --> 00:46:31.719
And it turned out that I was attending<br/>another event being held by NTTA.

00:46:31.820 --> 00:46:35.080
At the same time the<br/>NTTA people were arriving,

00:46:35.820 --> 00:46:37.180
the children would have been leaving.

00:46:37.180 --> 00:46:39.880
So unfortunately they had to<br/>end their celebration

00:46:39.880 --> 00:46:45.440
early so there wouldn't be that danger<br/>of kids crossing the parking lot as all

00:46:45.440 --> 00:46:46.719
of these others were coming in.

00:46:46.719 --> 00:46:50.300
So I suggested to them that they<br/>look at Mountain View College.

00:46:51.460 --> 00:46:54.680
Because it's larger,<br/>they've got more parking lots, etc.

00:46:55.239 --> 00:47:00.200
So the director, Ana Lorena Carrasco,<br/>thanked me on Friday for opening

00:47:00.200 --> 00:47:01.420
those doors in Mountain View.

00:47:01.420 --> 00:47:05.880
Because they did have a huge celebration,<br/>hundreds of kids and parents.

00:47:05.880 --> 00:47:08.739
And as you know,<br/>that's a great opportunity to

00:47:08.739 --> 00:47:11.840
expose those parents,<br/>and also the children,

00:47:12.500 --> 00:47:15.120
to our campuses and what it is<br/>that we have to offer.

00:47:15.560 --> 00:47:18.760
But I think that when we<br/>have community events like that,

00:47:18.940 --> 00:47:20.739
where people are coming to us,

00:47:21.200 --> 00:47:23.739
I don't know what kind<br/>of communications happen

00:47:23.739 --> 00:47:26.820
so that our outreach people know.

00:47:27.360 --> 00:47:30.320
So that they can minimum<br/>maybe provide some bags,

00:47:30.540 --> 00:47:33.580
definitely with some information<br/>about our programs,

00:47:33.580 --> 00:47:34.000
etc.

00:47:34.000 --> 00:47:36.580
But I think if we're<br/>not making those connections

00:47:36.580 --> 00:47:39.600
on outreach when they're actually<br/>coming to us,

00:47:40.160 --> 00:47:43.900
we're losing opportunities to<br/>let people know

00:47:43.900 --> 00:47:45.920
broadly what it is that<br/>we do and what we have

00:47:45.920 --> 00:47:47.600
for them at our campuses.

00:47:48.540 --> 00:47:52.600
But so glad to know that our campuses<br/>are being used by our communities.

00:47:54.760 --> 00:47:56.219
Any other comments?

00:47:58.640 --> 00:48:05.620
Personally, I'd just like to restate<br/>the excitement around graduation.

00:48:05.920 --> 00:48:11.960
When I took this job four years ago,<br/>I had no idea of the impact that we have.

00:48:12.160 --> 00:48:16.800
But standing on stage and taking<br/>hands with all those

00:48:16.800 --> 00:48:19.600
students and looking their faces<br/>and seeing the parents,

00:48:20.160 --> 00:48:21.880
it's why we do this.

00:48:22.020 --> 00:48:23.900
And so it's special for me.<br/>I know it's special

00:48:23.900 --> 00:48:25.400
for all of us. It's special for you.

00:48:25.400 --> 00:48:29.380
So thank you, as the Chancellor said,<br/>to everyone who has happened.

00:48:30.780 --> 00:48:35.239
Summer break. We don't need a summer break.<br/>You're just ready to keep going.

00:48:35.520 --> 00:48:38.140
Now this is time to,<br/>like Grandpa used to say,

00:48:38.280 --> 00:48:39.900
time to scab over and heal up.

00:48:40.120 --> 00:48:45.500
And so we'll do a little bit of that.<br/>And it's a good time of the year.

00:48:47.520 --> 00:48:52.840
We have four folks I'd like to celebrate<br/>who are leaving us as retirees.

00:48:52.840 --> 00:48:56.840
And I think we just make it up<br/>for the size of the crowds.

00:48:56.980 --> 00:48:59.460
It would clap extra large for these folks.

00:48:59.880 --> 00:49:02.840
Lisa James spent 20 years with us. Lisa.

00:49:06.980 --> 00:49:09.719
Charlotte Short, 14 years.

00:49:13.280 --> 00:49:15.640
Alex Stradhagen, 24 years.

00:49:18.739 --> 00:49:21.380
And Glenstone, 37 years. Thank you.

00:49:25.370 --> 00:49:28.410
Thank you for your service,<br/>and we wish you the best wherever

00:49:28.410 --> 00:49:29.530
you are in the future.

